Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:43:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 86/86] XHTTP: Reach more of the flow governor from the model
 and the fuzzers

Half the protocol model runs send GOAWAY from step 100 to 500: a client
that changes its window ends most runs with the governor giving up long
before step 2500, so GOAWAY never met a changed window. A second fuzz
target drives a client's governor through Write and Read together and
answers its PINGs, so the round trip, the cuts that follow it and the
handover to a governed server run; the server target also runs with a
kernel that reports a queue.
